        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Update a SCIM user",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "url": "https://huggingface.co/api/organizations/:name/scim/v2/Users/:userId",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "name",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              },
              {
                "name": "userId",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "type": "json",
              "data": "{}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Updates a provisioned user, you'll need to provide all their information fresh - just like setting them up for the first time. Any details you don't include will be automatically removed, so make sure to include everything they need to keep their account running smoothly. Setting `active` to `false` will deprovision the user from the organization."
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Update SCIM user",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "url": "https://huggingface.co/api/organizations/:name/scim/v2/Users/:userId",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "name",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              },
              {
                "name": "userId",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "type": "json",
              "data": "{}"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Update an attribute of a SCIM user. Modify individual attributes using Operations format. Just provide the changes you want to make using add, remove (only `externalId` is supported), or replace operations.\n If you set `active` to `false`, the user will be deprovisioned from the organization. \nComplicated SCIM `path` values are not supported like `emails[type eq 'work'].value`."
        },
